From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:03:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qcow2: count the pending requests of each queue

Since each queue has its own QCOW2_REQS requests, qcow2_pending() returned
QCOW2_REQS minus the free requests of all the queues: a negative count when
the driver is idle, so tapdisk_vbd_quiesce_queue() always saw pending
requests and pausing a qcow2 VBD never completed.

Count the requests in use in each queue, under the lock of the queue, which
protects its free list.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/block-qcow2.c | 16 +++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block-qcow2.c b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
index 2744aeb7..9fb9827b 100644
--- a/drivers/block-qcow2.c
+++ b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
@@ -1529,14 +1529,16 @@ static int
 qcow2_pending(td_driver_t *driver)
 {
 	struct qcow2_state *s = (struct qcow2_state *)driver->data;
-	int n_pending;
-	unsigned int n_count = 0;
+	int n_pending = 0;
 
-	pthread_mutex_lock(&s->lock);
-	for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(s->queue); i++)
-	    n_count += s->queue[i].vreq_free_count;
-	n_pending = QCOW2_REQS - n_count;
-	pthread_mutex_unlock(&s->lock);
+	/* Each queue has its own QCOW2_REQS requests, protected by its lock. */
+	for (int i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(s->queue); i++) {
+		struct qcow2_queue *q = &s->queue[i];
+
+		pthread_mutex_lock(&q->lock);
+		n_pending += QCOW2_REQS - q->vreq_free_count;
+		pthread_mutex_unlock(&q->lock);
+	}
 
 	return n_pending;
 }
